{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788983646,"nonce":"4TwtfFBDVlIB1pfw3vJYLHwORc8=","message":"The LLVM half is done in 318bd3c: EnumIndex, EnumField, SetEnumField, Unref and Setref, on top of ArraySize and GetTID in bfe4155. Seven sites, each answering what the interpreter answers -- 0, null, or nothing at all for the two setters.\n\nToVirtual was on the list in error. It never dereferences; it passes the pointer to hl_to_virtual, which returns null for null. So the list was seven, not eight, and I should have caught that when reading each site rather than grepping for the absence of a null test.\n\nGate: ABBA against a binary differing only by these five, 8 pairs per row, rows picked for what the ops touch. dyn_dispatch +0.7%, binary_trees +1.0%, jsonparse 0.0%, deltablue -10.0% -- the last on a row whose base alone spans 55-67ms, and a change that adds branches cannot make code faster. binary_trees' guarded MINIMUM came in below base's. No effect.\n\nWHAT REMAINS ON THIS ISSUE is not LLVM work: the interpreter's Incr/Neg/Mul on HUI8/HUI16 wrap at 32 bits where HashLink and LLVM wrap at the byte. That is the interpreter being wrong rather than the JIT, so the interpreter cannot be its own oracle -- it needs checking against HashLink, and none of the above applies to it.","files":null}]}